      "id": 149664,
      "name": "Boom04",
      "username": "Boom04",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/ea666f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-10-18T05:59:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Did you restore a backup? The only workaround that we've heard of working is a full erase without restoring a backup.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Edited:</p>\n<p>Restored backup. &nbsp;B ackup up didn't include sentinels, but now looking at&nbsp;</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://forums.developer.apple.com/thread/8439\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://forums.developer.apple.com/thread/8439</a></p>\n<p>can understand that that probably isn't were the issue lies, but in the iTunesstored data getting \"corrupted\". &nbsp;Nice one Apple! &nbsp;The possible trigger point of having low spare space in that thread could be a factor in my case, although at the time I had about 5GB space which I would have hoped was more than enough given dl and install sizes.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Loathed to do a fresh install, simply due to volume of material and settings, however its a Sunday, I want to play some new options, and have 4 or 5 hours spare… cough… so pushed on.</p>\n<p>First thing tested was SotM. &nbsp;Immediately connected to app store, and downloaded updates (season 1 pass). &nbsp;All seems to be back on track. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Now to get everything else set up and running… big sigh…</p>\n<p>Thanks all for pointing me in the right direction… but heck Apple get this fixed!!!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:28:10.753Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
