      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"MigrantP\"]\n\nDid you restore a backup? The only workaround that we&#39;ve heard of working is a full erase without restoring a backup.\n\n[/quote]\n\n Edited: \n\nRestored backup. &nbsp;B ackup up didn&#39;t include sentinels, but now looking at&nbsp; \n\nhttps://forums.developer.apple.com/thread/8439\n\ncan understand that that probably isn&#39;t were the issue lies, but in the iTunesstored data getting &quot;corrupted&quot;. &nbsp;Nice one Apple! &nbsp;The possible trigger point of having low spare space in that thread could be a factor in my case, although at the time I had about 5GB space which I would have hoped was more than enough given dl and install sizes.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nLoathed to do a fresh install, simply due to volume of material and settings, however its a Sunday, I want to play some new options, and have 4 or 5 hours spare... cough... so pushed on.\n\nFirst thing tested was SotM. &nbsp;Immediately connected to app store, and downloaded updates (season 1 pass). &nbsp;All seems to be back on track. :-)\n\nNow to get everything else set up and running.... big sigh....\n\nThanks all for pointing me in the right direction...... but heck Apple get this fixed!!!\n\n&nbsp;\n",
